,"detail":"產品定價權增強，毛利結構健康"},{"id":9,"category":"營運效率","desc":"資產週轉率提升 (ΔTurnover > 0)","passed":1,"detail":"每單位資產產出效益改善"}],"fair_val":127.47,"default_fair_val":127.47,"premium_pct":-63.6,"is_undervalued":true,"pe_trailing":15.2,"pe_forward":13.4,"pb_trailing":4.5,"pb_forward":4,"div_yield":7.77,"ps_ratio":2.1,"fcf_to_ev":7.98,"fcf_to_mcap":11.73,"liab_to_assets":73,"cash_to_assets":0.6,"current_ratio":0.91,"roe":29.7,"roa":7.8,"moat":{"ticker":"WES","period":"2026Q2","m1_brand_pricing":{"score":3,"comment_zh":"Western Midstream Partners, LP 屬於油氣中游行業，其產品本質上是商品，缺乏獨特的品牌溢價能力。客戶選擇服務商時，價格和可靠性是主要考量，而非品牌忠誠度。因此，在定價權和品牌方面，其經濟護城河非常薄弱。公司無法像消費品公司那樣透過品牌建立顯著的定價能力，其收入主要取決於商品價格和運輸量，這使得其在 M1 維度上得分不高。","comment_en":"Western Midstream Partners, LP operates in the oil and gas midstream sector, where its products are essentially commodities lacking unique brand premium power. When customers choose service providers, price and reliability are the primary considerations, not brand loyalty. Therefore, its economic moat in terms of pricing power and brand is very weak. The company cannot establish significant pricing power through branding like consumer goods companies; its revenue primarily depends on commodity prices and transportation volumes, resulting in a low score in M1."},"m2_patents_regulatory":{"score":2,"comment_zh":"油氣中游行業的進入壁壘主要來自於基礎設施的建設成本和土地使用權，而非專利或獨特的技術。雖然行業受到嚴格的監管，但這些監管更多是為了安全和環境標準，而非賦予特定公司特許經營權。WES 的業務模式不依賴於專利技術，其競爭優勢也不來自於監管特許。因此，在專利和監管壁壘方面，其護城河幾乎不存在。","comment_en":"Barriers to entry in the oil and gas midstream industry stem mainly from infrastructure construction costs and land rights, rather than patents or unique technologies. While the industry is heavily regulated, these regulations are primarily for safety and environmental standards, not for granting specific companies exclusive operating rights. WES's business model does not rely on patented technology, nor does its competitive advantage come from regulatory franchises. Consequently, its moat in terms of patents and regulatory barriers is virtually non-existent."},"m3_high_switching_costs":{"score":7,"comment_zh":"對於油氣生產商而言，更換中游運輸和處理服務商的成本相當高昂。這涉及到鋪設新的管道、建立新的處理設施，以及重新協商供應鏈和合同。一旦與 WES 簽訂長期合同並使用其基礎設施，生產商通常會繼續使用，因為更換的初始投資和運營中斷風險巨大。這種基礎設施的綁定效應構成了顯著的轉換成本，為 WES 提供了一定的護城河。","comment_en":"For oil and gas producers, the cost of switching midstream transportation and processing service providers is considerable. This involves laying new pipelines, building new processing facilities, and renegotiating supply chains and contracts. Once a long-term contract is signed with WES and its infrastructure is utilized, producers typically continue to use its services due to the substantial initial investment and operational disruption risks associated with switching. This infrastructure lock-in effect constitutes significant switching costs, providing WES with a degree of moat."},"m4_network_effects":{"score":3,"comment_zh":"WES 的業務模式主要基於點對點的基礎設施連接，例如管道網絡。雖然一個龐大且相互連接的網絡可以提高效率，但其網絡效應並不像社交媒體或市場平台那樣，用戶越多，價值越高的情況。油氣生產商選擇服務商時，更看重單點的連接效率和成本，而非整個網絡的規模。因此，網絡效應對 WES 的護城河貢獻有限。","comment_en":"WES's business model is primarily based on point-to-point infrastructure connections, such as pipeline networks. While a large and interconnected network can enhance efficiency, its network effects are not like those of social media or marketplaces where more users directly increase value. Oil and gas producers prioritize the efficiency and cost of individual connections rather than the scale of the entire network when choosing service providers. Therefore, network effects contribute limitedly to WES's moat."},"m5_cost_advantage_scale":{"score":8,"comment_zh":"作為一家大型油氣中游公司，WES 受益於顯著的規模經濟效應。其龐大的基礎設施網絡（管道、儲存設施、處理廠）能夠以較低的單位成本處理大量的油氣。新建同等規模的基礎設施需要巨額資本投入，這對潛在競爭者構成了巨大的進入障礙。規模化的運營降低了單位運輸和處理成本，使其在成本上具有競爭優勢，這是其重要的護城河。","comment_en":"As a large oil and gas midstream company, WES benefits from significant economies of scale. Its extensive infrastructure network (pipelines, storage facilities, processing plants) can handle large volumes of oil and gas at a lower per-unit cost. Constructing equivalent infrastructure on a new basis requires massive capital investment, posing a substantial barrier to entry for potential competitors. Scaled operations reduce per-unit transportation and processing costs, giving it a competitive cost advantage, which is a significant moat."},"m6_unique_geography_assets":{"score":7,"comment_zh":"WES 在美國關鍵的油氣產區（如 Permian Basin）擁有廣泛且關鍵的基礎設施網絡。這些地理位置優越的資產，能夠高效連接生產商與煉油廠或出口終端，使其成為該地區不可或缺的物流樞紐。對於特定區域的生產商而言，WES 的管道網絡是其產品進入市場的最經濟、最可靠的途徑。這種地理上的集中和關鍵性構成了其獨特的資產壁壘。","comment_en":"WES possesses an extensive and critical infrastructure network in key U.S. oil and gas producing regions (such as the Permian Basin). These geographically advantageous assets efficiently connect producers to refineries or export terminals, making them indispensable logistics hubs in the region. For producers in specific areas, WES's pipeline network represents the most economical and reliable route to market for their products. This geographical concentration and criticality form its unique asset barrier."},"m7_operational_efficiency":{"score":7,"comment_zh":"WES 在運營效率方面表現出色，體現在其對基礎設施的有效管理、維護和擴張能力上。公司能夠以相對較低的運營成本處理大量的油氣流量，並確保服務的穩定性和可靠性。其較高的 ROE (29.7%) 和 ROA (7.8%) 也間接證明了其營運效率。持續的資本支出用於優化網絡和提高效率，這有助於維持其競爭優勢。","comment_en":"WES demonstrates strong operational efficiency, reflected in its effective management, maintenance, and expansion capabilities of its infrastructure. The company can handle substantial oil and gas throughput at relatively low operating costs, ensuring service stability and reliability. Its high ROE (29.7%) and ROA (7.8%) also indirectly attest to its operational efficiency. Continuous capital expenditure is directed towards optimizing the network and improving efficiency, which helps maintain its competitive advantage."},"m8_capital_allocation":{"score":6,"comment_zh":"WES 的資本配置策略似乎側重於基礎設施的擴張和維護，以及為股東提供穩定的股息。雖然其 FCF TTM (2,248.9M) 表現強勁，但其債務水平相對較高（$9,129.0M）。公司在平衡再投資、償還債務和股息支付方面需要謹慎。相較於一些專注於回購或戰略性併購的公司，其資本配置的靈活性和創造股東價值的潛力可能稍遜一籌。","comment_en":"WES's capital allocation strategy appears to focus on infrastructure expansion and maintenance, as well as providing stable dividends to shareholders. Although its FCF TTM ($2,248.9M) is strong, its debt level is relatively high ($9,129.0M). The company needs to be prudent in balancing reinvestment, debt repayment, and dividend payments. Compared to some companies focused on share buybacks or strategic acquisitions, its capital allocation flexibility and potential for shareholder value creation might be slightly less pronounced."},"m9_customer_retention":{"score":7,"comment_zh":"如 M3 所述，由於更換成本高昂，油氣生產商與 WES 的合作關係通常具有較高的黏性。一旦生產商的設施與 WES 的管道網絡連接，並依賴其進行運輸和處理，他們很難輕易轉向其他服務商。這種基礎設施的綁定效應，加上 WES 在關鍵地區的市場地位，使得客戶留存率相對較高，構成了穩固的護城河。","comment_en":"As mentioned in M3, due to high switching costs, the relationship between oil and gas producers and WES typically exhibits high stickiness. Once a producer's facilities are connected to WES's pipeline network and rely on it for transportation and processing, it is difficult for them to easily switch to other service providers. This infrastructure lock-in effect, combined with WES's market position in critical regions, results in relatively high customer retention rates, forming a solid moat."},"m10_durability":{"score":7,"comment_zh":"油氣中游行業的基礎設施具有長期使用的特性，其經濟壽命可達數十年。WES 的管道和處理設施一旦建成，便能持續產生現金流，只要能源需求持續存在。儘管面臨能源轉型和監管變化的長期風險，但短期至中期內，其核心業務的穩定性較高。其業務模式類似於「收費橋」，為能源運輸提供必需的服務，具有一定的持久性。","comment_en":"The infrastructure in the oil and gas midstream industry is characterized by long-term usability, with economic lifespans extending for decades. Once WES's pipelines and processing facilities are built, they can continuously generate cash flow as long as energy demand persists. Despite long-term risks from energy transition and regulatory changes, the stability of its core business is relatively high in the short to medium term. Its business model resembles a 'toll bridge,' providing essential services for energy transportation, possessing a certain durability."},"overall_moat_verdict_zh":"Western Midstream Partners, LP (WES) 的經濟護城河主要建立在其龐大的規模經濟（M5）和關鍵地理位置的基礎設施網絡（M6）之上。這些資產為油氣生產商提供了顯著的轉換成本（M3）和客戶黏性（M9），使其業務模式類似於能源運輸的「收費橋」。然而，其產品的商品屬性限制了定價權（M1），且不依賴專利或特許經營（M2）。雖然運營效率（M7）和資產的持久性（M10）尚可，但其資本配置（M8）需關注債務水平。總體而言，WES 擁有中等偏上的護城河，主要依賴於基礎設施的網絡效應和轉換成本。","overall_moat_verdict_en":"Western Midstream Partners, LP (WES) possesses an economic moat primarily built upon its significant economies of scale (M5) and its network of infrastructure assets in key geographic locations (M6). These assets create substantial switching costs (M3) and customer stickiness (M9) for oil and gas producers, rendering its business model akin to an energy transportation 'toll bridge.' However, the commodity nature of its products limits pricing power (M1), and it does not rely on patents or regulatory franchises (M2). While operational efficiency (M7) and asset durability (M10) are adequate, its capital allocation (M8) requires attention to debt levels. Overall, WES exhibits an above-average moat, largely driven by infrastructure network effects and switching costs.","evidenceHash":"68d1ce5344f4afaf5022c974b00a41bbac0bfbec791628792db223743e65c021","assessmentPolicy":"buffett-moat-v3","model":"gemini-2.5-flash-lite","provider":"Vertex AI"},"ratingSources":{"moat":{"reason":null},"fScore":{"score":6,"checkedAt":null},"zScore":{"asOfDate":"2025-12-31","period":"FY 2025","basis":"comparableAnnual","model":"z","zone":"distress","reason":null,"scoringCurrency":"USD","applicability":null,"checkedAt":"2026-10-31T06:51:39.344Z","evidenceHash":"fb09658aafacb100861e4fe76dd597ba962af4b84e123f0722748797502c101b"},"mScore":{"asOfDate":"2025-12-31","period":"FY 2025","basis":"comparableAnnual","model":null,"zone":"clean","reason":null,"scoringCurrency":"USD","applicability":null,"checkedAt":"2026-10-31T06:51:39.344Z","evidenceHash":"fb09658aafacb100861e4fe76dd597ba962af4b84e123f0722748797502c101b"}},"fin_valuation":{"is_financial":false},"image":"https://images.financialmodelingprep.com/symbol/WES.png","logo":"https://images.financialmodelingprep.com/symbol/WES.png","website":"https://www.westernmidstream.com","ceo":"Oscar K. Brown","full_time_employees":"1704","description":"Western Midstream Partners, LP, an energy infrastructure company operating with its subsidiaries, primarily acquires, owns, develops, and manages assets across the United States. Its core functions include the collection, compression, treatment, processing, and transportation of natural gas. The firm also handles the gathering, stabilization, and conveyance of condensate, natural gas liquids (NGLs), and crude oil, alongside the collection and disposal of water generated during production. Additionally, it engages in the buying and selling of natural gas, NGLs, and condensate. Western Midstream maintains operations in significant regions such as Texas, New Mexico, the Rocky Mountains, and north-central Pennsylvania. Western Midstream Holdings, LLC functions as its general partner. Formed in 2007, the company is headquartered in The Woodlands, Texas, and rebranded from Western Gas Equity Partners, LP to its current name in February 2019.","description_en":"Western Midstream Partners, LP, an energy infrastructure company operating with its subsidiaries, primarily acquires, owns, develops, and manages assets across the United States. Its core functions include the collection, compression, treatment, processing, and transportation of natural gas. The firm also handles the gathering, stabilization, and conveyance of condensate, natural gas liquids (NGLs), and crude oil, alongside the collection and disposal of water generated during production. Additionally, it engages in the buying and selling of natural gas, NGLs, and condensate. Western Midstream maintains operations in significant regions such as Texas, New Mexico, the Rocky Mountains, and north-central Pennsylvania. Western Midstream Hold